(2) GENUS-BLINDNESS:  (-1)^{F(R)-1} == (-1)^m  for ALL rotation systems R
     (checked exhaustively over even-series sigma at k<= 3)
   genus-blindness holds for all 403 (sigma,R) checked: True
======================================================================
Interpretation: the per-ribbon-map sign (-1)^{F-1} sees only the cycle rank m,
NOT the genus.  So no genus-0 restriction can recover C_k (ADDENDUM-4 routes).
S_k is the N=-1 evaluation of an ALL-GENUS rooted-map sum; the loop equation
xF^2+F=1 must come from a Tutte/root-edge recursion, not a planarity filter.
